    "updated_at": "2023-10-10T14:32:55Z",
    "body": "> @nt1m the website can already read out the password, no? A subset of user agents already supported `dirname` there too, including WebKit. And removing password support from that seemed more risky to me. (This is also discussed in the linked issues.)\n\nThis isn't about the website being able to read the password, but more about changes in directionality being reflected as you type the password, which is a bad UX imo, unless I'm misunderstanding the implications of the dir=auto change.",
